 ## Subtopics
 
 ### Relative Gaussian Deformation Network
-A network that calculates changes in logical coordinates $\Delta w$ during mesh deformation, allowing Gaussians to roam on the mesh surface rather than being anchored to a facet [S1, unofficial]. It takes the mesh embedding $E_M$, the vertex embeddings of the three vertices of the facet containing Gaussian $i$ ($E_{V1}, E_{V2}, E_{V3}$), and the Gaussian's current logical coordinate $w_i$ as input, outputting $\Delta w_i$ [S1, unofficial].
-Formula: $\Delta w_i = \text{RGD}(E_M, E_{V1}, E_{V2}, E_{V3}, w_i)$ [S1, unofficial].
+Calculates changes in logical coordinates $\Delta w$ during mesh deformation, allowing Gaussians to roam on the mesh surface rather than anchor to a facet [S1, unofficial]. It takes $E_M$, the vertex embeddings of the containing facet ($E_{V1}, E_{V2}, E_{V3}$), and the Gaussian's current logical coordinate $w_i$ as input, outputting $\Delta w_i$ [S1, unofficial]. Formula: $\Delta w_i = \text{RGD}(E_M, E_{V1}, E_{V2}, E_{V3}, w_i)$ [S1, unofficial]. Choose this variant when Gaussian position drift relative to the mesh surface is required for accurate dynamic reconstruction [G]. See also [Deformation Network (Dynamic)](16182-deformation-network-dynamic.md).
 
